title: Political Rally
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: rally_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rally_timer = 6
card-image: img/protest.jpg
go-to: main_rally; sa_disrupt if sa_strength > 180 and not sa_banned and not return_to_normalcy

@sa_disrupt

The Nazi SA has disrupted our rally! Their street troops are preventing us from meeting.

- @rfb_protect: Use the RFB to protect our rally.
- @cancel: Cancel the rally.

@rfb_protect
on-arrival: rfb_success = rfb_strength*rfb_militancy - sa_strength*sa_militancy; strife += 1
go-to: rfb_protect_win if rfb_success >= 0; rfb_protect_lose if rb_success < 0

@rfb_protect_win
go-to: main_rally

The RFB has successfully protected our rally against the SA! Our meeting can go ahead as usual.

@rfb_protect_lose
on-arrival: workers_nsdap += 3; rfb_strength -= 50

Unfortunately, the RFB was not able to hold back the SA mob. The Nazis have won this show of strength.

@cancel
on-arrival: workers_nsdap += 3;

The SA have won this show of strength.

@main_rally

Mass rallies are a common feature of social democratic life, especially in the lead-up to an election. What is the primary theme of this rally?

- @class_struggle: The immediate revolution of the proletariat against the bourgeoisie.
- @welfare: Sozialpolitik - the maintenance and expansion of social welfare programs.
- @communism: Establishing a communist state modeled after the USSR.
- @pacifism: Opposing war, nationalism, and militarism at all costs.
- @local: A mixture of various local and national concerns that resonate most with the audience.
- @easy_discard

@class_struggle
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if ultra-left_strength > right_strength; workers_kpd += 4*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress > 0; unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress > 0; ultra-left_strength += 5; ultra-left_dissent -= 5

Our message of class struggle is supported by the whole party. [? if nationalization_progress > 0 : Our achievements in nationalization have assisted our messaging. ?]

@welfare
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare > 0; unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare > 0; unemployed_kpd += 4*(1-dissent) if welfare > 1

The reformist message appeals to the organized workers, whose benefits are the accomplishments of social democracy. [? if welfare > 1 : Our achievements in expanding welfare have made this message more effective. ?]

@communism
on-arrival: democratization -= 1; pro_republic -= 2*(1 - dissent); workers_kpd += 4*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; pro_republic -= 4*(1 - dissent)

Our speakers expound the communist system against the bourgeois capitalism and parliamentary democracy.

[? if democratization > 3 : Talk of communism does not excite the workers as much as more practical issues. But that may change; part of our job is to provide political education to the proletariat. ?]
[? if democratization <= 3 : Since there is low support for the democratic republic, the workers are enthusiastic about our message. ?]

@pacifism
on-arrival: pacifism += 1; nationalism -= 2*(1 - dissent); workers_spd += 4*(1 - dissent) if pacifism >= 3; unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if pacifism >= 3; nationalism -= 3*(1-dissent)

Our speakers denounce the reactionary military establishment and all the spending entering that black hole. Some adventurous speakers question the responsibility of the military elites in organizing the Great War.

[? if pacifism < 3 : Given the volume of nationalist indoctrination in our society, it is difficult to argue so vehemently against the military. ?]
[? if pacifism >= 3 : Since we have consistently made pacifism a theme of our campaign, the workers are enthusiastic about our message. ?]

@local
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent);

Our speakers have gauged the mood and are speaking to the issues that seem to most affect the workers in this moment.
